# Data conversion between byte and kilobyte

Verifies direct data conversion between byte and kilobyte in both directions. Forward, converting 1B to 0.001KB with a fractional finer-to-coarser scale promotes the integer result to decimal, while 1.5B yields 0.0015KB; backward, converting 1KB to 1000B preserves the integer representation across the integer coarser-to-finer scale, while 1.5KB yields 1500.0B.

>>> source
forward_whole: int = 1B
print(forward_whole->to(KB))
forward_fractional: decimal = 1.5B
print(forward_fractional->to(KB))
backward_whole: int = 1KB
print(backward_whole->to(B))
backward_fractional: decimal = 1.5KB
print(backward_fractional->to(B))

<<< stdout
0.001KB
0.0015KB
1000B
1500.0B

<<< stderr
